  "status": "present",
  "value": "feasibility is monotone in k, so binary search the smallest feasible k (k * e1 - (n - k - 1) * e2 > 0, or k = n); scan k upward from there, cutting a stair walk off once it reaches the best time and stopping when k * t1 + (n - k) alone reaches the best, since every stair floor costs at least 1. Complexity target: O(log n + n^2) worst case time/O(1) space.",
